Key findings:

F1 (A1.9 L1-L4). The B7 commit rewrote the mathd CLI, ledger, and added an
independent Python verification oracle (check_b7_ledger.py using CPython's
`json` and `hashlib` modules). The oracle verifies: (1) JSON escaping/round-trip
of tricky claims, (2) strict one-line-per-failed-claim format in the mistake
ledger with {timestamp, claim, counterexample} schema, and (3) SHA-256 hash
chaining of ledger entries. All three checks pass independently of the Rust test
suite.

F2 (A1.10 mutation sweep). The 50-mutant sweep (tools/mutate-mathd.py) achieved
88.0% mutation score: 44 mutants killed, 6 survived. The surviving mutants
(M04, M09, M35, M38, M48, M50) indicate oracle gaps particularly in the
canonicalizer (M35, M38 — hash comparison/chaining) and ledger (M48 — hash
chain, M50 — timestamp format) modules. The full sweep log is at
docs/logs/mutate-sweep.log.

F3 (B7 mathd red on musl). The historical CI runs 42264120829 and 42267064190
failed because `test_python_independent_ledger_oracle` in tests/ledger.rs runs
check_b7_ledger.py, which previously looked only for
mathd/target/debug/mathd-cli. Under `--target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl`, Cargo
outputs binaries to mathd/target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/mathd-cli,
causing check_b7_ledger.py to raise RuntimeError when locating the CLI binary.
This is an oracle-path issue, not a kernel or build failure.

F4 (A1.1 fix resolution). The A1.1 fix ("Fix mathd-cli lookup in check_b7_ledger
for musl target", commit 7ab7781) added find_cli_cmd supporting
MATHD_CLI_BIN env var, target-specific debug paths (including musl), and fallback
discovery in mathd/target. The red CI run log was committed as
docs/logs/a1-mathd-red-42267064190.log. The green CI run 42390240969
confirms the fix landed and the mathd test suite passes: `cargo test` successful,
all 37 tests ok, clippy and fmt --check clean.

No changes to .github/workflows/check.yml required: existing step runs
  python -m unittest tests/test_recovery.py -v (for F1.12 D4) and separate
  mathd CI steps are unaffected.

F5 (mutate-sweep.log comparison). The generated docs/logs/mutate-sweep.log
documents the 50-mutant sweep from A1.10: total 50, killed 44, survived 6
(M04, M09, M35, M38, M48, M50). This log did not exist prior to this review;
it is now committed as an evidence file.

